{{!-- Shared per-section edit pencil/done toggle, used by the character Details
      sections and the steading sections. Caller passes `toggleClass` (the
      context-specific hook the sheet's click handler keys on), `section` (the
      section id) and `editing` (that section's effective edit state). Shown only
      when the sheet is editable and the global edit wrench is OFF (when it's on,
      every section is already editable). The `recentlyEdited` faded branch is a
      no-op for callers that don't populate `stonetop.recentlyEdited`.

      A caller that also wants the fold caret passes `collapse` — the id to
      remember the fold under. It is deliberately its own id, not `section`: two
      move groups share the edit section "moves" but fold independently. Opt-in,
      so a section with nothing worth hiding (or its own collapse already, like
      the Arcana headings) simply omits it.

      The sheet's switches are read off the partial's own context and, failing that, off @root: a
      caller inside an {{#each}} (a homebrew insert's tab, drawn once per insert) has the insert as
      its context, and without the fallback its moves had no pencil at all. --}}
{{#if (or stonetop.canEdit @root.stonetop.canEdit)}}
{{#unless (or stonetop.editMode @root.stonetop.editMode)}}
{{#if editing}}
<a class="stonetop-section-done {{this.toggleClass}}" data-section="{{this.section}}" title="Done editing"><i class="fas fa-check"></i></a>
{{else}}
{{#if (lookup (or stonetop.recentlyEdited @root.stonetop.recentlyEdited) section)}}
{{!-- Just left edit mode: a non-interactive check that fades out, then a
     re-render swaps in the hover pencil below. --}}
<a class="stonetop-section-done {{this.toggleClass}} steading-section-toggle-faded" tabindex="-1"><i class="fas fa-check"></i></a>
{{else}}
<a class="stonetop-section-edit {{this.toggleClass}}" data-section="{{this.section}}" title="Edit: make this section editable"><i class="fas fa-pencil"></i></a>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{/unless}}
{{/if}}
{{!-- The caret sits to the RIGHT of the pencil (both float in the section's
      top-right corner) and reveals on the same hover. Outside the canEdit /
      editMode gates above: folding a section is a reading preference, so it is
      there for a player looking at someone else's sheet too. The open/shut
      state and the `stonetop-section-collapsed` class on the wrapper are
      applied by _wireSectionCollapse, not here. --}}
{{#if collapse}}{{> "stonetop.section-collapse" collapse=collapse}}{{/if}}
